From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brad Barnett <127794626+bdbarnett@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 24 Nov 2026 00:00:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] esp32: the heap leaves room in PSRAM for TLS and the network.

The esp32 port's heap grows on demand. When an allocation fails after a
collection, gc_try_add_heap() adds an area as big as the whole heap so far,
capped only by gc_get_max_new_split(), which was ESP-IDF's largest free
block. On an S3 with 8 MB of PSRAM, the step after a 4 MB heap took all of
the PSRAM that was left, and an area goes back to ESP-IDF only when nothing
at all lives in it. Builds that give mbedTLS PSRAM only
(CONFIG_MBEDTLS_EXTERNAL_MEM_ALLOC), or move Wi-Fi and lwIP buffers there,
then had nowhere to put a TLS session: an HTTPS request failed with
gc.mem_free() reporting megabytes free.

gc_get_max_new_split() now also stops short of the last
MICROPY_GC_SPLIT_HEAP_SPIRAM_RESERVE bytes of free PSRAM, 256 KB unless a
board sets its own (0 turns it off). Builds without PSRAM are unchanged.
With PSRAM, the heap no longer grows into internal RAM once PSRAM is down
to the reserve, which keeps that RAM for DMA buffers and task stacks;
gc.mem_free() counts the reserve as not free.

On a Waveshare ESP32-S3-Touch-LCD-7 (8 MB octal PSRAM), filling the heap
with 4 KB objects and freeing 31 of every 32 left 33 KB of PSRAM, and the
next TLS handshake failed. With this change the same run grows the heap to
6.4 MB, leaves 210 KB of PSRAM free, and the handshake succeeds; three TLS
sessions held open at once on top of it left 87 KB.
---
diff --git a/ports/esp32/gccollect.c b/ports/esp32/gccollect.c
index e6c17fda6..f9aa690ef 100644
--- a/ports/esp32/gccollect.c
+++ b/ports/esp32/gccollect.c
@@ -80,9 +80,22 @@ void gc_collect(void) {
 #if MICROPY_GC_SPLIT_HEAP_AUTO
 
 // The largest new region that is available to become Python heap is the largest
-// free block in the ESP-IDF system heap.
+// free block in the ESP-IDF system heap. With PSRAM, it is also no more than
+// leaves MICROPY_GC_SPLIT_HEAP_SPIRAM_RESERVE of PSRAM free, so the heap can't
+// take the room ESP-IDF allocates from there.
 size_t gc_get_max_new_split(void) {
-    return heap_caps_get_largest_free_block(MALLOC_CAP_DEFAULT);
+    size_t avail = heap_caps_get_largest_free_block(MALLOC_CAP_DEFAULT);
+    #if CONFIG_SPIRAM && MICROPY_GC_SPLIT_HEAP_SPIRAM_RESERVE > 0
+    size_t spiram_free = heap_caps_get_free_size(MALLOC_CAP_SPIRAM);
+    size_t spiram_avail = 0;
+    if (spiram_free > MICROPY_GC_SPLIT_HEAP_SPIRAM_RESERVE) {
+        spiram_avail = spiram_free - MICROPY_GC_SPLIT_HEAP_SPIRAM_RESERVE;
+    }
+    if (avail > spiram_avail) {
+        avail = spiram_avail;
+    }
+    #endif
+    return avail;
 }
 
 #endif
diff --git a/ports/esp32/mpconfigport.h b/ports/esp32/mpconfigport.h
index 1243955a2..b41d75aea 100644
--- a/ports/esp32/mpconfigport.h
+++ b/ports/esp32/mpconfigport.h
@@ -103,6 +103,14 @@
 #define MICROPY_GC_SPLIT_HEAP               (1)
 #define MICROPY_GC_SPLIT_HEAP_AUTO          (1)
 
+// PSRAM that the Python heap never grows into, kept for ESP-IDF's own
+// allocations there: mbedTLS sessions, and Wi-Fi, lwIP and Bluetooth buffers
+// on boards that move them to PSRAM. Without it, the heap's growth step can
+// take all of the PSRAM that is left. A board can set its own, or 0 for none.
+#ifndef MICROPY_GC_SPLIT_HEAP_SPIRAM_RESERVE
+#define MICROPY_GC_SPLIT_HEAP_SPIRAM_RESERVE (256 * 1024)
+#endif
+
 // extended modules
 #ifndef MICROPY_PY_ESPNOW
 #define MICROPY_PY_ESPNOW                   (1)
